  "body": "In one of the last commits, probably around 1d5f38a9d594b7d9871cef4fbe35c4859a0ec94e, when the -R command line option was removed, also the -s option disappeared, not listed among changes in any issue (at least that I could find). I was using that option and found it very convenient for opening single raw files without triggering the file browser. Now, if I open a single raw file, ART correctly opens in editor mode, but it also keeps scanning the current directory for generating thumbnails. In directories with many files this can be a problem: if I try to close ART before thumbnails are generated, in fact, it locks for awhile and then it crashes.",
